    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d29">

                <pb facs="0087" n="61" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v04/pg61"/>

                <head>29. Memorandum of Telephone Conversation Between the Secretary of State and
                    the President’s Special Assistant for National Security Affairs (Bundy)<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d29-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1963-08-30T18:08:00-04:00"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">August 30, 1963—6:08
                    p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">TELEPHONE CALL FROM MR. BUNDY</p>
                <p>Sec returned the call and B asked if Sec had fun with Alphand.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d29-f2"/> Sec said he claims and he will say to the press this was a
                    long-term view and it is almost what our Pres said in 1961 re Viet-Nam.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d29-f3"/> B asked if Sec has seen Lodge’s report on his call
                    on French Ambassador Lalouette.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d29-f4"/> Sec said yes. B
                    thinks it is interesting and raised the question of whether Cabot should talk to
                    these people more concretely than he has especially if the other plan is a
                    fallen balloon. B said we can’t settle it tonight but thought he would mention
                    it. We may need this channel. B does not think he has told them very much except
                    we are disturbed. We will reread them. This is one subject that was not <pb
                        facs="0088" n="62" xml:id="pg62"/> discussed this p.m. Sec mentioned Madame
                    Nhu’s coming here. Agreed this is ominous. B said if Cabot told the French Amb
                    they should go that went to the Nhus. Sec will study it this evening and B will
                    too. Meeting tomorrow at 11.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
